/** Standalone batch AE -- new 4-case standard (Sample + boundary + tricky + stress).
 * All solvers below were independently written and verified byte-for-byte against each problem's
 * real official Sample before being trusted to generate boundary/tricky/stress expected output.
 *
 * uva-815-flooded: each grid square is a 10m x 10m (100 m^2) area, so cubic-meter volume = 100 *
 *   sum(level-elev) over submerged cells -- an actual bug caught while verifying against the real
 *   sample: solving with the RAW volume (without the /100 area scaling) produced water levels roughly
 *   100x too high. Binary search on the (real-valued) water level, since flood volume is monotonic in
 *   level.
 * uva-820-internet-bandwidth: standard undirected max-flow (BFS augmenting-path Ford-Fulkerson);
 *   undirected edges modeled as capacity added to BOTH directions in an adjacency-matrix residual
 *   graph, which also correctly sums multiple parallel connections between the same pair of nodes.
 * uva-828-deciphering-messages: greedy left-to-right scan; m (the rule-3 position counter) carries
 *   across word boundaries WITHIN THE SAME MESSAGE LINE (spaces are skipped but never reset or advance
 *   m) -- resetting m per word was an actual bug caught while verifying against the real sample's own
 *   multi-word message. A character matching L[m] is a valid rule-3 triple start only if the character
 *   2 positions ahead matches L[m+1] (and neither is a space); otherwise it's decoded as a literal
 *   rule-2 character. "error in encryption" is detected when a LITERAL decode produces a letter that
 *   is itself an L-member (impossible under rule 2, which only ever encodes non-L letters) -- treating
 *   a failed triple-match as an unconditional hard error instead (a plausible-looking alternative) was
 *   tried and rejected because it broke several real-sample messages that decode validly via the
 *   literal-then-inL-check path.
 * uva-834-continued-fractions: standard Euclidean-algorithm expansion (b_k = floor, remainder becomes
 *   the next denominator), with a defensive last-coefficient-merge (if the final term is 1, fold it
 *   into the previous term via the [...,a,1]=[...,a+1] identity) to guarantee bn>1 as required, even
 *   though it was never observed to trigger on real Euclidean-algorithm output in practice.
 * uva-846-steps: derived a closed form independently -- for k steps (start/end length 1, adjacent
 *   lengths differing by at most 1), the maximum reachable distance is floor((k+1)^2/4) (a symmetric
 *   "ramp up then down" shape), and the achievable-distance range for a given k is contiguous down to a
 *   value low enough (steps can dip to length 0) that the answer is simply the smallest k with
 *   floor((k+1)^2/4) >= d -- confirmed against all 13+ cases in the real official sample.
 * uva-855-lunch-in-grid-city: Manhattan distance separates into independent street and avenue
 *   components, each minimized by its own MEDIAN (any median minimizes sum of absolute deviations);
 *   ties (even friend count) are broken toward the LOWER of the two central values per the problem's
 *   own stated rule.
 * uva-865-substitution-cypher: each dataset's first two lines (the substitution table) are print in
 *   SWAPPED order verbatim, with NO substitution applied to them -- confirmed directly against the real
 *   sample, where translating them would have given a different (wrong) result in one of the datasets.
 *   Every subsequent line (including a line that happens to duplicate the "from" string as plain text)
 *   is translated character-by-character through the from->to table, with characters outside the table
 *   passed through unchanged.
 */
